    "title": "What channel is the Final Four on today? TV schedule, stream, time",
    "text": "April 4, 2026, 7:02 a.m. CTThe college basketball season has arrived at the Final Four.Arizona, Michigan, UConn and Illinois won their regions in the 2026 men’s NCAA Tournament to punch their tickets to Indianapolis where their dreams of a national title remain alive.The Final Four on Saturday, April 4, begins with UConn, a two seed out of the East Region, playing Illinois, a three seed from the South Region, followed by top seeds Arizona (West) and Michigan (Midwest) squaring off to close out the action inside Lucas Oil Stadium.UConn (33-5) is making its third Final Four in the last four years and eighth overall - all since 1999 - following the team’s improbable 19-point comeback win over Duke in the Elite 8 sealed by Braylon Mullins’ last-second three-pointer that put his name forever in the March Madness collection of magical moments. The Huskies have a good track record in the Final Four. UConn has advanced to the title game in six of their seven appearances in the Final Four, with back-to-back championships most recently in 2023 and 2024.While UConn knows all about Final Fours, this is a new territory for Illinois (28-8). The Illini are in their first Final Four since a Deron Williams and Dee Brown-led team had Illinois in the title game in 2005.Arizona (36-2) and Michigan (35-3) in the nightcap features two of the most dominant teams all season. The Wildcats, winners of the Big 12 regular season and tournament titles, is in its first Final Four in 25 years. Arizona enters the weekend fresh off the news that its head coach, Tommy Lloyd, has signed a contract extension keeping him in Tucson through 2031.Arizona began the year 23-0 and after its only two losses on the season in the second week of February, the Wildcats bring a 13-game winning streak into the Final Four. Its two defeats this season came by a combined seven points.Michigan is making its ninth appearance in the Final Four (though two of them have been vacated by the NCAA) and first since 2018. The 2026 Michigan team won the Big Ten with only one loss - to Wisconsin - and has dominated the opposition in the tournament, throttling Tennessee by 33 points in the Elite 8.Will it be an all-Big Ten final to guarantee the conference’s championship drought ends, will UConn ride the momentum to another title game and can Arizona reach its first final since 1997?Here’s where to watch the Final Four games, including TV and streaming info, the start times and an updated bracket:Who's playing in the Final Four?Two No. 1 seeds, a No. 2 and a No. 3 make up the 2026 Final Four.Arizona (1)Michigan (1)UConn (2)Illinois (3)What time is the Final Four? Final Four start timesIllinois vs UConn, 5:09 p.m., Saturday, April 4Michigan vs Arizona, 7:49 p.m. Saturday, April 4Times above are CentralWhat channel is the Final Four today? Where to watch the Final Four on TVTV: TBS and truTVLive stream: Stream the Final Four on Sling TV.The Final Four games air on TBS and truTV and stream on SlingTV.Stream the Final Four on Sling TVWho is favored in the UConn vs Illinois game? Odds, spreadSpread: Illinois -2Total: 139.5 pointsMoney line: Illinois -135, UConn +115Odds courtesy of BetMGMWho is favored in the Arizona vs Michigan game? Odds, spreadSpread: Michigan -1.5Total: 157.5 pointsMoney line: Michigan -120, Arizona +100Odds courtesy of BetMGMMarch Madness bracketHere's the NCAA Tournament bracket:[UPDATED PRINTABLE NCAA TOURNAMENT BRACKET]When is the national championship game 2026?The winners of the two Final Four games will play in the national championship game on Monday, April 6, back at Lucas Oil Stadium.Tipoff is set for 7:30 p.m.Who was in the Final Four last year?Last year's Final Four featured all four No. 1s: Florida, Auburn, Duke and Houston.Florida beat Auburn in one semifinal, and Houston stunned Duke with an incredible comeback in the other to advance to the title game.Who won March Madness 2025?The Florida Gators won the national championship in 2025. The Gators overcame a 12-point second-half deficit to defeat Houston, 65-63, for their third title and first since winning back-to-back championships in 2006 and 2007.March Madness winners, NCAA Tournament championsHere are the last 10 national champions:2025: Florida2024: UConn2023: UConn2022: Kansas2021: Baylor2020: N/A2019: Virginia2018: Villanova2017: UNC2016: Villanova2015: Duke",
